{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/391901-middlewhere-requiem-forum-group","id":391901,"title":"Middlewhere Requiem - Forum Group","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-03T15:16:24-08:00","id":391901,"title":"Middlewhere Requiem - Forum Group","content":"Dear Members,<br /> <br /> I want to invite interested parties to join a Vampire the Requiem (2nd Edition) Forum game that is currently underway using the Proboards Forum system. We are looking for interesting and unique individuals that are wanting to tell a story and be part of a world that is focused on inter-connected tales of kindred in Chicago. While knowledge of the system is always important, it is more important to love story telling and being an actor in your own story and the stories of others for this forum.<br /> <br /> At this moment we have 3 story tellers that are contributing to the forum and playing NPCs that make up the vast majority of the background. We are making sure the focus is always on the character\u2019s story, and not a global plot that masks and shadows the characters. The transition to the new system has just been completed as well, meaning all characters are starting on the same foot in terms of experience and progression.<br /> <br /> The majority of players are located in Indiana and know one another fairly well, but we are all very accepting and welcoming. This is not a forum that will push bias and conformity, or huddle in small cliques. The players on the forum enjoy, and encourage, creative role-play that ushers in new experiences for our players. If you think you might be interested, please send me a <u>private message on here or email me at <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#711d041210025f101f150314065f1304051d140331161c10181d5f121e1c\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"731f061012005d121d170116045d1106071f160133141e121a1f5d101c1e\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a></u>.<br /> <br /> Sincerely,<br /> Aodhfin (Lucas)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 Storyteller for the <a href=\"http://middlewhere.boards.net\" target=\"_blank\">Middlewhere: Chicago Requiem</a> Forum<br /> \u2022 Graphic and Creative Designer","edited":{"userid":4927,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4927-aodhfin","user":"Aodhfin","date":". 02-19-2015, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4927-aodhfin","name":"Aodhfin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4927_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T15:23:51-08:00","id":412149,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://middlewhere.boards.net\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u><b>Middlewhere: Chicago Forum</b></u></span></a><br /> <br /> <b>Player Population</b>: 8-15 Players (Active and Semi-Active)<br /> <b>Status</b>: <b><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Currently Accepting New Players</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Middlewhere: Chicago - Setting</b><br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The Greater Chicago Court Gathering Introduction</b> </div> </div> </div></div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">On the evening of the New Moon, an exclusive all-night gala is held at the Chicago Theater. Glittering with gold, no expense is spared. Dazzling performances, enticing delicacies, and irresistible prestige draw the most beautiful, wealthy, and powerful Kindred and kine of The Second City. Hosted by the Invictus and held to their exacting standards, the Kindred who attend range from upstarts to high-ranking members of City, Clan, and Covenant.<br /> <br /> The lobby of the Chicago Theater is a spectacle of sin, decorated to immortal tastes and exquisite design. The area is caked in rich and vivid dark colors: lurid sensuality drips from the banisters wrapped in fine crimson and gold, and chaises of rich velvets and silks and leathers are centuries old. The individuals in the lobby ooze as much depravity and decadence as the structure itself, as some whisper in hushed tones and others speak in brash and lustful rasps. The bodies of the individuals grind and sway together to the allure of sublime music, some doing a waltz for two while others lure new prey into their seductive grasps.<br /> <br /> Through the lobby, the guests find the theater itself filled with those who are admirers of the finer arts. Soft and stimulating dances and songs are sung by both mortal and immortal performers. While some may speak and ridicule or admire, unvoiced dramas and intrigues unfold in the shadowed corners. The private back rooms and lounges are seemingly unguarded -- and where those of higher status find themselves, in lavish dens bursting with carnal desires.</span></i> </div> </div> </div><br /> The 'Middlewhere: Chicago' forum is set in a game that is focused on the interconnected stories of the kindred within the city and the horrors of world that they find themselves in direct contest with. The kindred must navigate a dark sea of hungry fangs and eyes, all waiting for the opportune moment to strike and exact their unjust prizes. They will face off against one another and more infamous entities of the World of Darkness; this includes, but is not limited, to the Strix, The Unholy, Solomon Birch, Sir Hermann of the Invictus, Hunters, and many other famous figures from the canon material.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Middlewhere: Chicago - Format</b><br /> <br /> <br /> The format we use is a \u2018Play-by-Post\u2019 system, in which players will take turn posting as their characters in various threads on the forum. This is best described as \u2018Turn-based writing\u2019, where characters will interact with one another by posts. The difference between Chat and Forum RP is that Forum RP does not always occur over real-time; posting may occur every few seconds, or over the course of hours.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The majority of players are writers, or creatives by profession, and post lengths will vary from 2-5 sentences to multi-paragraphs posts.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The contents of the forum are mature, dark, and violent at times. All players are of 18 years of age, at minimum.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The Forum is focused exclusively on the Vampire the Requiem setting, for player characters, and will only for player characters to be Mortal, Ghouls, or Kindred.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The characters are all created using the same creation process, which is augmented to reflect more experienced and weathered kindred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 Storyteller for the <a href=\"http://middlewhere.boards.net\" target=\"_blank\">Middlewhere: Chicago Requiem</a> Forum<br /> \u2022 Graphic and Creative Designer","edited":{"userid":4927,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4927-aodhfin","user":"Aodhfin","date":". 02-19-2015, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4927-aodhfin","name":"Aodhfin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4927_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}